# EduExplained (repo: campus-publication)

EduExplained answers practical education questions, pre-K through doctoral, across the United States. Pages are built by a pipeline of narrow agents (`.claude/agents/`), each loading only the skills it needs (`.claude/skills/`). Code orchestrates everything between agents. This file loads into every session, so it holds only what every session needs; everything else lives in skills.

## Rules for every session
- Never read, print or edit any `.env` file.
- No em dashes anywhere, in pages, code comments or docs.
- Facts come only from `intel/<topic>/facts.csv`. Forum posters are never sources.
- Validate every handoff file before finishing: `python3 scripts/validate_handoff.py schemas/<name>.schema.json <file>`.
- Stay inside the files your task names. Don't edit other agents' outputs.

## Where things live
| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `intel/<topic>/topic.json` | topic brief from the topic scout |
| `intel/<topic>/raw/` | researcher notes, one file per lane |
| `intel/<topic>/facts.csv` | the fact file, single source of truth |
| `intel/<topic>/readers.json` | reader map |
| `intel/<topic>/usecases.json` | use-case hierarchy and reader matrix |
| `intel/<topic>/coverage/<slug>.json` | what each page must answer |
| `intel/<topic>/search/<slug>.json` | search brief per page |
| `intel/<topic>/layers/<slug>.json` | layer plan per page |
| `build/packets/<slug>.json` | the writer's packet, built by code |
| `content/articles/<topic>/<slug>.md` | published pages |
| `content/checks/<slug>.json` | checker results |
| `content/index.json` | every live page (slug, title, query, topic) |
| `data/inventory/<area>.json` | dataset inventories |
